{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implementation pushed as Gerrit change 1575 (option B, per the 2026-08-07 operator ruling).\n\nWhat landed in `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_cloud_rate_limit_sweep_heldout.py` (no production code touched):\n\n- `_SWEPT_TRANSPORT_MODULES` — the four transport paths are now a named constant consumed by `_step0_names()`, so the sweep's declared subject is a reviewable artifact rather than a literal buried in a helper. Still exactly four modules; no package-wide glob (AC1).\n- `_unswept_jira_modules()` — DERIVES the guard's scope as the package listing minus the swept set minus `__init__.py`, so `acli_subprocess.py` and `jira_fields.py` (both missing from earlier hand-written scope notes) are covered, and a module added beside the four is covered the day it lands (AC2).\n- `_is_pure_transport_facade()` — the AST predicate. Admits only `return self.transport.<same name>(args forwarded unchanged)`, optionally preceded by a docstring. Rejects extra statements, guards, retries, logging, argument transforms, dropped/reordered args, non-transport or renamed targets, `*args`/`**kwargs` passthrough, async defs, and no-return bodies. Scans at any nesting depth so a nested class cannot hide a mutation (AC3).\n- `_KNOWN_BENIGN_COLLISIONS` — the accepted set is asserted to be EXACTLY `backend.py::set_relationship` and `backend.py::add_comment`; a new accepted facade is a deliberate 429-policy decision, not drift (AC4).\n- 15 rejection fixtures plus one acceptance fixture (AC5). Mutation-checked against the real tree as well: appending a non-facade `add_comment` to `jira_fields.py` turns `test_antidrift_unswept_classified_collisions_are_only_pure_transport_facades` RED naming `jira_fields.py::add_comment`; reverting restores green.\n- `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and the whole `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler` suite (2410 tests) pass (AC6).\n\nOn the AC3 rewording the operator required in the same change: it was already applied to the description by the EDIT event at 1786293886890275001, which replaced the original glob-only criterion with the option-B wording now in the ticket (current AC3 = the pure-facade acceptance rule; current AC5 = drift detection over the declared transport surface). Verified against the CREATE event's original text, so no further description edit was needed. Plan review PASSED with 0 blocking findings and was signed before claim."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786313875639627001,"uuid":"f97445f7-67ae-4fa3-b3fb-4e34cc76e399"}